From: pocket-debs
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:31:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Allocate the output buffers outside the CMA area
Description:
 The software ISP allocates its output buffers from the first dma-buf
 provider it can open, the CMA heap before the system heap. At 4620x3472 an
 XRGB8888 output buffer takes 61 MiB; with the default four buffers the 128
 MiB CMA area of the Motorola Moto G60s, shared with the display and the raw
 capture buffers of a camera without IOMMU, runs out after the first buffer.
 .
 The output buffers are written by the CPU or the GPU and read by the
 application. Take them from the system heap, falling back to udmabuf.
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-19
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp
index c73a16c..590d5f0 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp
@@ -82,8 +82,13 @@ LOG_DEFINE_CATEGORY(SoftwareIsp)
 SoftwareIsp::SoftwareIsp(PipelineHandler *pipe, const CameraSensor *sensor,
 			 ControlInfoMap *ipaControls)
 	: ispWorkerThread_("SWIspWorker"),
-	  dmaHeap_(DmaBufAllocator::DmaBufAllocatorFlag::CmaHeap |
-		   DmaBufAllocator::DmaBufAllocatorFlag::SystemHeap |
+	  /*
+	   * The output buffers are written by the CPU or the GPU and read by
+	   * the application, nothing needs them physically contiguous. Keep
+	   * them out of the CMA area, which on devices without an IOMMU for
+	   * the camera DMA has to hold the raw capture buffers.
+	   */
+	  dmaHeap_(DmaBufAllocator::DmaBufAllocatorFlag::SystemHeap |
 		   DmaBufAllocator::DmaBufAllocatorFlag::UDmaBuf)
 {
 	if (!dmaHeap_.isValid()) {
